<%#
  The year is a marker over the rows, not a second rail. Giving it its own
  168px column stacked two margins — year at the page edge, dates a further
  168px in — and opened a gap down the middle of the archive. Set at the left
  edge it shares a column with the dates below it, which is what makes the
  listing read as one ledger.
%>

<section class="mb-9 border-t border-slate-6 pt-4">
  <h2 class="m-0 mb-2 text-title text-slate-12 tabular-nums">
    <%= @title %>
  </h2>

  <%#
    Every entry carries its own bottom hairline, so the last row's rule plus
    the next group's top rule doubled every boundary with dead space between
    them. A one-row group made it obvious; it was happening at all of them.
    The group's own top rule is the boundary.
  %>

  <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0 [&>*:last-child]:border-b-0">
    <%= content %>
  </div>
</section>
